Z||000000||jd2m4||11-25-2001||12:50 AM||||Let me start off by saying how great it is to find people that like the fiero as much as i do. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">I'm in the process of buying back my 85 2m4 from a friend i sold it to.I'd like to mod to iron duke,But was wondering if it would just be more cost-effective to find a 2.8 v-6 to mod and put in,and what all has to be changed to swap in a v-6? Also,What 2.8's can be used?Does it have to be one from a front wheel drive platform,Or can any 2.8 be used? Thanks for the help. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000001||Spiff||11-25-2001||01:01 AM||||Welcome to the forum.<P>It may be easier to start with a V6 car. I think you need to get the wiring harness, ECM, and obviously the complete engine. Others will have a better breakdown of what's needed to do the conversion. <P>If you do get the 4 cyl and put a V6 in it, I would get a 93-95 Camaro/Trans Am 3.4 pushrod motor and put all the Fiero parts from the heads up on it. You will only have to move the starter to the other side of the engine. Which should not be that hard. You should contact Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory on Toney, Alabama about your plans. He will help you out.<P>Sorry so long winded. Again welcome to the forum.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig_1.gif"> <P>Jon<P>	My Baby's<BR>						  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula  T-Top  # 1008 of 1252  (5 Spd White/ Grey)<BR>1988 Fiero Coupe    T-Top  #      31 of 1252  (5 Spd   Red / Grey) SOLD<BR>	<BR>	and the rest<P>2000 Ford Ranger 4x4<P>York, Pa 17404<BR>MAFOA||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||11-25-2001||09:51 AM||||Hey, welcome... as another member once stated, your engine options or limited by your ambition, oh and some $'s.||||reg||1
